WEBVTT

NOTE FINAHQ and Munshi, a two-minute overview. Illustrative data throughout: every company and figure is fictional.

1
00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:05.251
This is FINAHQ, with Munshi. One platform that runs your entire close.

2
00:00:07.355 --> 00:00:12.116
Fifty entities. Five different ledgers. And a deadline that doesn't move.

3
00:00:13.351 --> 00:00:22.165
Every night, FINAHQ pulls trial balances, ledgers and subledgers from SAP, Oracle, NetSuite, Dynamics and QuickBooks.

4
00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:32.912
Munshi, your AI finance agent, reconciles intercompany balances, explains every difference, and drafts the eliminations for your approval.

5
00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:36.361
Leases are covered too.

6
00:00:36.111 --> 00:00:44.153
Under IFRS 16 or US GAAP, FINAHQ builds every schedule, posts the journals, and feeds the disclosures.

7
00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:53.114
Then it consolidates every level, from entity to region to group, and you can drill from any number straight to the account behind it.

8
00:00:55.353 --> 00:00:59.694
Slice any figure by location, cost centre, product or segment.

9
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:05.822
Standard statements and board packs are ready from day one.

10
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:19.459
And with custom templates, you get your complete financial statements, every note and every disclosure, in exactly the format your auditors expect.

11
00:01:21.352 --> 00:01:26.938
Munshi also prepares your audit working papers, each one tied back to the trial balance.

12
00:01:31.352 --> 00:01:38.230
And through the FINAHQ connector for Claude, your team can just ask, and get answers computed from your own books.

13
00:01:41.355 --> 00:01:47.085
Run it in your own cloud if you prefer. SOC 2 is expected by March 2027.

14
00:01:48.351 --> 00:01:53.284
Pull, reconcile, consolidate, report and audit. All in one platform.

15
00:01:55.373 --> 00:01:58.514
FINAHQ and Munshi. Book a demo today.
